Status: NOT_STARTED - deferred backlog; do not begin without a new request.
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/1
Milestone: Smooth, responsive gameplay on phones without sacrificing sharpness.
Dependencies: None; preserve the completed71 full-resolution contract.

Purpose:
Address the owner's report that the website performs abysmally on a phone,
playing at approximately10FPS. This is a user-reported symptom, not an
independently measured baseline or an established root cause.

Tasks:
- [ ] Reproduce on agreed physical phones and record device/browser/game,
      sustained gameplay FPS, frame times and audio/input behavior.
- [ ] Profile native emulation and the 3D scene separately to locate the
      actual bottlenecks before choosing optimizations.
- [ ] Improve the measured bottlenecks while retaining71's device-aware
      pixel density, sharp LCD, artwork, geometry and existing controls.
- [ ] Compare before/after real-phone results and verify audio, touch,
      loading, saves and desktop behavior remain correct.
- [ ] Record measured results and update affected documentation.

Acceptance criteria:
Agreed target phones sustain native-speed gameplay with responsive controls
and usable audio, supported by recorded before/after measurements. A narrow
desktop viewport alone is not phone-performance evidence. Do not silently
lower resolution, change native game speed or weaken existing quality gates
to manufacture a performance improvement.

Completion evidence:
None. Only the owner's approximately10FPS report is recorded. No phone
benchmark, profiling, optimization or runtime verification has been started.

Completion log:
2026-11-06: Owner requests this future TODO and explicitly says not to work
on it now. Register the backlog item only; await a new implementation request.
